WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.760
Don't miss that brightly shining light!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.870
It's always there beside you.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:26.420
I'm sure the rest just depends on your perception.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.590
You don't have to search for it—just notice that it's there!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.350
There's a tenderness that lies hidden behind the most common things:

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:43.230
a light that showers our days in color!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.230
Tiny Days: This world is constructed...

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.800
Tiny Days: ...by fragments of miracles!

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.180
Things that seemed meaningless

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.730
were actually protecting us, loving us, more than we ever knew.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.960
Tiny Heart: Our feelings flow forth...

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Tiny Heart: ...as we give thanks for everything we've been given.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.490
We'll never, ever forget...

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.700
We'll cherish this feeling forevermore!

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.000
The Pep Rally

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.710
Getting a little faster won't be enough for you to beat me!

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.250
I <i>will</i> win!

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:55.260
Verrill Shot Launcher:
Tornado Typhoon Cyclone Slash!

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.760
That was too easy.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.820
You're awesome, Gourai-kai!
Now finish her off, Gourai-kai!

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:24.740
Well done. This Gourai-kai upgrade of yours has its benefits.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.710
Gourai-kai! This has been a splendid first battle!
Well done, Gourai-kai!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.870
And I did all the assembly. Pretty awesome, right?

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.090
I did it all by myself, without Bukiko's-

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:38.840
Hooray, hooray, Gourai-kai!
Do your best, Gourai-kai!

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.780
Gourai-kai can win this.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.620
Please win, Gourai-kai.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:42.720
Go, go, Gourai-kai! Go, go, Gourai-kai!

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.770
Hey, don't ignore me! I put in a lot of work! Hey!
Go, go, Gourai-kai! Go, go, Gourai-kai!

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:51.020
Go, go, Gourai-kai! Go, go, Gourai-kai!

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.020
Dammit!

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.570
So fast!

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.170
Go, go, Gourai-kai! Go, go, Gourai-kai!

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:22.970
Damn... it!

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.600
This is the end!

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.170
Winner: Gourai.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.240
Architect! Are you all right?

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.330
Copy Mode. Code: Hresvelgr. Complete.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.670
Gourai, it was a sound victory.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.830
Thank you, Architect.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.320
Mission complete.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.840
Great work!

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.220
Thanks to your data,
I was able to battle a virtual Hresvelgr.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.470
I'm grateful.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.680
It was nothing.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.810
And your new armor is perfect!

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.920
Yes. I'm extremely pleased with the finished product. Thank you, Ao.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:17.560
And thanks to all of your help,
next time I will beat her!

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.900
I suggest we hold a talent show,
to show support for the rematch that is to come!

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.820
Ooh, that would be great. Like a pep rally!

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.080
Let's all support her!

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.580
Yeah!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.930
From Baselard and Stylet,
the "Miracle Magical Illusion Show"!

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.560
Clap, clap!

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:28.030
For my first trick, I shall pierce this box with swords.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.660
I'm in quite a pinch!

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.160
It's quite frightening, isn't it?
Will she be all right?

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.960
That tickles!

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.400
H-Hey! Behave yourself!

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.420
Okay.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.550
F.A. Girl!

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.720
The box has now been pierced with all ten swords.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.000
Does Baselard remain unharmed?!

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.350
Ah! I'm caught on this part here.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.390
Shh! Don't say that!

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.640
Very well, Charger-kun: Come on!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.530
Huh? What do I do next again?

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.080
Don't tell me you forgot! You get out, right?

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.460
Oh. Yeah, yeah.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:15.680
Do you even remember how?

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.330
Sure, no problem. I've got this!

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:22.750
So, will Baselard be able to get out in one piece?

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.960
One, two, three!

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.420
Base, are you okay?

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.840
Hang on a second...

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.250
Ta-daa! The magic totally worked!

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.970
Wow!

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:42.480
Can that even be called...

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:43.850
..."getting out"?

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.560
Gourai! Do your best in your revenge match!

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:47.940
I'm sure you can do it!

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.820
Thank you very much.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.510
This was Stylet and...

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:53.240
...Base, thanks!

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.300
F.A. Girl!

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.700
Continuing on - it's Architect!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:00.660
Her performance will be a celebratory song.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.420
Learning Mode: Opera. Replay.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:19.810
<i>The light is pouring in at dawn.</i>

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:28.070
<i>Let's forget about our hardships for a moment,</i>

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:35.090
<i>and celebrate victory.</i>

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.950
That's wonderful!

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.160
Analyzing virtual battle data.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:47.660
In a second bout between Gourai and Hresvelgr,
Gourai's chance of victory stands at 99.9999998%.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.380
Per program parameters, this can be viewed as 100%.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.800
Put simply, you are sure to win.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.550
Coming from you certainly makes it sound trustworthy!

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.720
It is based on a number of data samples.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.430
Gourai, you will win. Be encouraged.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.810
Thank you very much. I <i>will</i> win!

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:06.680
F.A. Girl.

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:10.770
And now, it's time for Program number four,
featuring the Materia Sisters.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:12.000
Their performance is...

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.530
Thank you.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.340
I'm Materia White.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:17.700
I'm Materia Black.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.040
Together, we make Materia Gray.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.120
Are you kidding me?

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.760
Say, Black-chan, do you know the "Ten times quiz"?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:32.340
Yes, of course.

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.780
Then say "pizza" ten times.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.970
Did you just give me an order?

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.180
When you think of autumn...

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.300
...you think of sports.

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:50.480
Black-chan, what would you say is the hardest exercise you've done recently?

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.020
I can't say. It's too stimulating.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.530
Go on, just say it.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:57.110
I rolled over on top of Charger-kun in my sleep.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.830
I can't contain myself. This is genius!

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:09.960
F.A. Girl.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.460
That's enough already.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.140
Fine, then I shall cease.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.090
Thank you very much.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.670
Splendidly done! Bravo! World class!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.720
What <i>was</i> that just now?

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.810
It was definitely hard to process...

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:24.980
Gourai-chan.

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:25.800
Yes?

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:29.810
No matter what condition you find yourself in, you'll be fine so long as you are confident.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.940
And you'll be sure to win.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:37.240
I've come to think so too. Thank you very much!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.150
F.A. Girl!

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:43.620
Now then, to finish us out,
here's our extra-special guest: Gourai's master, Ao!

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.250
I wrote a letter to Gourai that I'd like to read.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:58.380
"Dear Gourai, My life has changed a lot since you showed up.

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:02.470
At first, it was just about collecting battle data for money.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.820
To be honest, it still really helps me out!

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:08.280
Seriously, thank you for coming to my home.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:10.520
I couldn't be more grateful.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:13.020
But aside from that, I think of something else...

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:17.610
I'm happy when you win, and I'm sad when you lose.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:23.800
If your company said they needed data of you losing,
I'd do it for the money, of course!

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:26.040
But the truth is, I wouldn't like it.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:32.580
Incidentally, I was a little concerned when I realized this still doesn't convey how I feel.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.380
We're both girls and we live together.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:39.010
Doing battles all the time isn't too exciting.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.590
Let's go out more often, and have fun together...

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:45.010
But to do that, we'll need some cash!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:48.350
That's why you have to beat Hresvelgr.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:49.850
I'll do my best too.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.480
Basically, keep going, okay?

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:55.440
Do your best, Gourai! Go, go, Gourai!"

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.860
And, done!

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.280
Ao... thank you so much!

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.360
Uh, I'm not so convinced...

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.110
That friendship burns bright indeed.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.080
Indeed!

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.720
It looks like Ao-chan just whisked her away at the end!

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:10.900
Well, she is Gourai-chan's master after all.

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.830
We can forgive her for today.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:15.940
Finally, there's a special surprise!

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:17.580
I'll play you the trumpet!

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:18.250
Huh?

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:23.970
I've hid this up till now, but I've been in the Brass Band Club since elementary school.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.420
Oh, really?

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.010
Huh. I didn't know you could play an instrument.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.100
Ao, you're so cool! You're the real deal!

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.000
Ao-chan is wonderful. That suits her.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.020
I'm tingling with anticipation.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:39.730
Well, she did put Gourai-kai together,
so she's surprisingly good with her hands, huh?

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:43.610
This is truly a case of the hawk having hidden its talons.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:48.760
Meaning: one with talent or ability does not display such skill lightly.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:50.620
In other words: a hidden talent!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.000
Ao, I'm very happy.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:56.500
Well, here goes!

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:06.930
Autumn Beckons...

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:10.270
It's totally autumn now, isn't it?

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.810
Yes, it is.

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.310
Oh no.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:20.110
The "Limited Quantity, First-Come, First Served" special at Inage-ya hasn't started yet,

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.040
but I'm already hungry!

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:23.400
Will you be all right?

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.490
Let's go get a little snack.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.160
It's so delicious!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.950
Eating dango outside is the best!

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.410
Does it taste different when eaten outside the house?

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:36.580
It's the atmosphere, I guess.

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:40.880
Eating it under the sky and with this scenery
makes it feel like it tastes different.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.880
I see.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.760
Even though it's the same dango... Intriguing.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.840
Hey, Gourai, you want to go for a walk?

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:49.760
Yes.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:54.480
But it we don't hurry,
won't the special at Inage-ya be over soon?

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:58.140
They have two of them daily.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:00.270
I'll just change plans and go to the one at night.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:05.320
We used to take class trips to this park a lot when I as a kid.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:06.820
Oh, Really?

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.280
This sure is nostalgic!

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:11.280
Nostalgic...

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.290
Let's go on this.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:19.920
I sure was happy to have some
sweet rolled egg in my boxed lunch!

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:24.670
Though, I still can't decide if a banana constitutes a snack or not...

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:29.380
When I was a kid, I used to look forward to the boxed lunches more than the autumn leaves...

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:31.640
not that I can say I'm any different now.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:35.900
This area is a mountain of treasures!

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.330
A mountain of treasures?

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:39.850
There are all these acorns on the ground, right?

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.160
Acorns! They're pretty, aren't they?

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:46.620
When I was a kid,
I used to love using acorns to play house.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.650
What does it mean to "play house"?

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.530
Oh, you don't know what it is?

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.320
How can I explain...?

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:56.620
You decide who'll be the mother and the child,
and you pretend to be a family.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.180
A pretend... family?

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:00.710
I want to try!

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:01.800
Huh? For real?

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.400
Let's do it! I must!

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:04.580
No, no way.

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:05.880
Why not?

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.970
Um, high school students don't normally play house.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.390
Please! I want to know what a family feels like!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.010
Oh, yeah...

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.640
Well, when you put it that way, let's give it a shot.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.640
Thank you very much!

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:23.470
Well, I'll play the mom, so you be the child.

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:24.820
Understood.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:27.480
Gourai-chan! Dinner's ready.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.860
Here you go.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:31.240
Oh. Sorry for the bother.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:35.200
Gourai-chan, you're still young,
but you talk like a grownup, don't you?

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.870
Oh! Um... Thank you.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.210
Huh? You said you wanted to do this, but are you blushing?

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.540
Ah! U-Um, Ao!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:44.540
"Ao"?

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.150
You mean, "Mom"!

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:47.710
M-Mom...

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.550
Gourai-chan, say "Ah."

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:54.840
Well, Mom is going to make some pancakes for a snack.

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.260
Will you help?

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:57.390
Yes!

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:02.230
It's quite tiring, isn't it? This "playing house."

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:04.400
It was a lot of fun when I was younger.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.360
I'm an only child.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:10.940
Plus, my parents were always doing things together, so I spent a lot of time playing alone.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:12.360
Really?

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:18.790
I'm glad they always got along so well, but for Mom to go to Dad's work too...

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.080
that was kinda shocking.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:24.920
Speaking of, where did your mother and father go?

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.420
They're on the ocean!

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.340
The ocean?

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:32.820
My dad's the captain of a luxury cruiser that goes all around the world. That's his job.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.340
Oh, yes?

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:38.100
That's why they named me "Ao", for the blue sea.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:42.100
Apparently, it's Ao and not Umi because my parents decided to put their own twist on it.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:48.110
Since way back, they've always brought me masks and weird souvenirs from around the world.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.360
Now, though, I flat-out refuse!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.030
We used to come here sometimes,

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:56.320
but they were the ones who ran around acting like kids.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.160
Still, it was fun.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:02.660
Is that what mothers and fathers are like?

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.600
No, I think mine are a little different.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:08.680
I'd like to meet them sometime, your mother and father.

00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:12.510
Oh, yeah. I wonder what they'd say it they saw you.

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:14.300
Let's play!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:23.560
Huh? Who are you?

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.860
Hi! I'm Guriko!

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:26.920
Guriko?

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:28.530
I'm Gourai.

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:30.690
I want to play house too!

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:34.190
Okay, Gourai, it's dinnertime!

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.780
Dinner again?

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.660
Does it taste good?

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.780
Yes. It's delicious, Mom.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.910
Gourai, you're a good little girl.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:47.050
I've come to learn that playing house tends to follow a pattern.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:48.540
You may be right.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.820
Now it's time for your bath.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.250
Bath?

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:53.920
It's an acorn bath!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:55.260
A bath...

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.880
I've never experienced one before.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.300
Let alone an acorn bath.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:03.180
Shake, shake! Shake, shake!

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.480
I feel dizzy.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.850
Shake, shake!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.360
"Shake, shake"?

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.270
Shake, shake.

